## Commit

`4945410 feat: run deterministic CANSLIM diagnosis experiments`

## Concerns

The diagnosis APIs intentionally reject locked evaluation and D5 composition.  D5 remains controller-owned and needs two measured parent hashes supplied by that controller.  The full current-exit reason breakdown is immutable baseline authority for diagnosis; discovery and validation remain separately partitioned and no 2025 execution is available through the default runner.

The full repository suite was also attempted as part of branch finalization.  It stops at the pre-existing, unrelated `tests/test_agent_loop.py::test_task3_source_snapshot_reads_only_approved_candidate_text`: the sandbox denies `resolve()` access to a temporary controller directory under `C:\Users\llong\AppData\Local\Temp`.  The failure occurs in `agent_loop._validate_controller_temp_parent`, not in Task 6 files; the focused Task 6 suite remains green after the commit.

## Round 1 review corrections

The runner now requires a `BaselineReproduction` whose manifest identities match the context snapshots and whose exact comparison is verified before any D1–D4 run.  D0 remains the only default path available before that context state exists.

Experiment metrics now come from a deterministic replay that materializes cache facts, evaluates `CachedDiagnosisStrategy` at each exact row, queues only next-session opens, and runs `DiagnosisPortfolioSimulator` exit behavior.  The replay hash binds emitted signals, entry outcomes, and transactions.  Rule variants therefore alter the actual entry funnel (the RS-85 regression proves this).

`D4.CURRENT_EXIT_PACKAGE` reads terminal trades from the verified baseline snapshot's transaction ledger and partitions them by exit date.  It cross-checks the immutable 225-trade full-period cluster (97 stop, 92 MA, 30 time, 6 end; MA 15.22% / -2.86%) and rejects ledger tampering.  The removal variant preserves stop, scale-out, and protective-stop behavior while omitting only time-stop and EMA exits.

Promotion checks now include all non-worse return/annualized/Sharpe/drawdown and PIT-recall checks, strict improvement, fidelity, D0 reproduction, and sample floors.  Catalog resume checks identity and deserializes the atomic checkpoint before reading facts or invoking a runner; an incomplete batch is materialized once and reused.

