## Round 2 review corrections

Both direct experiment dispatch and catalog dispatch now run the same verified-D0 guard: the supplied `BaselineReproduction` must be passed, must bind to the authority/reproduced snapshot manifest hashes, and must still pass `compare_reproduction`.  A raw context containing a forged `passed=True` reproduction cannot bypass the guard.

D4 reads its transaction ledger only after checking the immutable snapshot's normalized transaction-row SHA-256 and, when present, the artifact file SHA-256.  Current-package trade statistics, exit attribution, and performance all derive from the same verified, partition-filtered terminal-trade population; cache replay equity is not mixed into those D4 metrics.  The immutable full-period exit cluster remains an additional cross-check.

Promotion now consumes `partition_baseline_performance` and `partition_baseline_recall` context evidence.  Missing partition references make their checks false; return, annualized return, Sharpe, drawdown, recall, and strict improvement are actual comparisons against the matching partition, never against the full-period snapshot.

