## Round 3 review corrections

D4 portfolio performance is no longer populated from a completed-position average.  It now requires the snapshot-artifact-hash-bound `equity_curve.csv` partition series with date, portfolio, benchmark, and cash values; it computes total and annualized return, Sharpe, drawdown, average cash, and benchmark deltas from that one series.  If the required verified partition series is missing, malformed, or lacks cash, D4 emits no performance evidence and all performance/promotion checks fail closed.

The canonical partition baseline performance and recall mappings are now represented in `promotion_evidence_sha256`, which is included in the experiment/checkpoint identity.  A resume under changed promotion evidence produces a different identity and does not reuse the prior result.

