## Round 5 review correction

D4 now reads cash exposure from the baseline producer's authoritative,
manifest-hash-bound `weekly_holdings.csv`, while continuing to read portfolio
and benchmark returns from the three-column `equity_curve.csv`.  It validates
the real `Week_Ending`, `Cash`, and `Total_Equity` fields, partitions weekly
observations to the requested D4 partition, and reports the hand-defined
`mean(Cash / Total_Equity) * 100`.  Missing, empty, malformed, out-of-order,
duplicate, negative, or impossible cash evidence fails closed with no D4
performance evidence; a holdings artifact hash mismatch is rejected.

`PerformanceEvidence.average_cash_pct` is required and finite again.  The
non-predeclared `average_cash_available` promotion gate was removed; average
cash remains reported evidence and does not independently satisfy strict
improvement.  The versioned complete-result and checkpoint digests are
unchanged and continue to cover the now-required cash value.

